    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`BUILD SUCCESS` \u2014 all tests green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key and duplicate detection for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**identityKey is now a SHA-256 hex digest.** `OwnerIdentity.key(telephone, email, lastName)` returns the lower-case hex SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` (a 64-char hex string), replacing the old pipe-delimited `telephone|email|householdId` string. The `postcode` parameter is gone.\n\n**New `Soundex` helper** \u2014 a standard American Soundex implementation (`src/.../function/owner/Soundex.java`), since no soundex/commons-codec existed in the project.\n\n**Duplicate detection (409) uses the single identity key.** `RequireUniqueIdentity` now compares full identity keys instead of the old telephone+email `contactKey`. It still skips soft-deleted owners, and the email-domain blocklist still runs earlier (in `RequireOwnerFields`), so a blocked address is rejected first. There is no separate householdId-based 409 block \u2014 because telephone is in the key, two owners with the same lastName+postcode but different telephones now have different keys and are not rejected.\n\n**Soft-match now keys on soundex + postcode.** `FlagPossibleDuplicate` flags a possible duplicate when the identity key differs but `soundex(lastName)` and postcode match an existing (non-deleted) owner \u2014 so same-household/different-telephone owners are created as soft matches rather than rejected. Declared household members are still never flagged.\n\n**Supporting updates:** `OwnerMapper` drops the `postcode` argument from the `identityKey` expression, and the `openapi.yml` `identityKey` field doc/example were updated to the new SHA-256 form.\n\nResults: `AcceptanceTest` (both `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity`) and the full suite pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\nNote: I left `OwnerIdentity.contactKey` removed (it was only used by `RequireUniqueIdentity`); the `AssignCustomerCode` customer-code hash is unchanged and still uses `normalizedTelephone`.",
